      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Citrus packing became Weirsdale’s economic backbone after groves sprouted in the 1870s and a railway opened in 1883.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weirsdale%2C_Florida",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Weir supplied water for irrigation, fishing, and early steamboat routes, drawing settlers to its eastern shores in the 1850s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/weirsdale_florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Weirsdale sits where State Road 25 meets State Road 42, anchoring it within the Ocala Metropolitan Statistical Area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
